    {
      "target_argument_id": "arg_93b6e2b8",
      "ground": "The argument erroneously cites Article 8(2)(b)(i) of the Rome Statute as the authority for the legal principle that wilful killing of civilians is not excused by military necessity.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(b)(i) defines wilful killing as a war crime but does not contain the legal test for distinguishing military from civilian targets or the military necessity exception. Relying on this provision to support the interpretive leap to genocidal intent is a misapplication of authority; the provision establishes the existence of the crime, not the specific intent to destroy a group.",
      "severity": "material",
